types.doc:
A gg call that failed.

Thrown by every function in this SDK. Catch it when a failure is expected and branch on `code`; let it escape when it is not, and gg reports which call failed and where your program was.

```
try {
    view.openText("notes", fs.readTextFile("notes.md"))
} catch (failure: ToolError) {
    if (failure.code == ToolErrorCode.NOT_FOUND) fs.writeFile("notes.md", "") else throw failure
}
```

It is a `RuntimeException`, which is what Kotlin makes every exception: there are no checked exceptions in this language, so a composed program is not forced into a `try` around every line, and a surface where every call returned a `Result` would force a branch after every line instead.
